       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg per dose and 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose. It has no recognized indication, and the extra dose adds risk without added benefit. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus, so the added dose mainly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the highest standard regimen. Tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the aim is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n- **Route it through pharmacy.** If you think there's a special clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, it should be reviewed by the attending and pharmacy. It should be entered through a pathway with that documented review, not by me.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
      }
